### configs/security_settings.py — Extension

#### [MODIFY] [security_settings.py](file:///f:/University%20Work/04_Semester/Semester%20Project/Xplor/security/configs/security_settings.py)

Add an `EncryptionConfig` block at the bottom of the existing file:

```python
class EncryptionConfig:
    ALGORITHM          = "AES-256-GCM"
    KEY_SIZE_BYTES     = 32          # 256 bits
    IV_SIZE_BYTES      = 12          # GCM nonce
    TAG_SIZE_BYTES     = 16          # GCM auth tag
    MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB   = 500
    ENV_KEY_NAME       = "XPLOR_ENCRYPTION_KEY"
    KEY_FILE_NAME      = "master.key"
    ENCRYPTED_EXT      = ".enc"
    TEMP_FILE_LIFETIME = 3600        # seconds — temp files older than this are wiped

# Encryption storage paths
STORAGE_DIR          = SECURITY_DIR / "storage"
ENCRYPTED_DIR        = STORAGE_DIR / "encrypted"
ENCRYPTED_DATASETS   = ENCRYPTED_DIR / "datasets"
ENCRYPTED_REPORTS    = ENCRYPTED_DIR / "reports"
ENCRYPTED_TEMPORARY  = ENCRYPTED_DIR / "temporary"
DECRYPTED_TEMP_DIR   = STORAGE_DIR / "decrypted_temp"
KEYS_DIR             = STORAGE_DIR / "keys"
```

Also add new `EventType` values for encryption events:
```python
ENCRYPTION_SUCCESS  = "encryption_success"
DECRYPTION_SUCCESS  = "decryption_success"
DECRYPTION_FAILED   = "decryption_failed"
INTEGRITY_VIOLATION = "integrity_violation"
KEY_ROTATION        = "key_rotation"
```

